<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daimler-Motoren-Gesellschaft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890–1926</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daimler-Motoren-Gesellschaft was a German engine and car maker founded in 1890 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottlieb-daimler">Gottlieb Daimler</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-maybach">Wilhelm Maybach</a> at Cannstatt near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a>. Its cars were sold under the name Mercedes from 1902, and in 1926 it merged with Benz &amp; Cie to form Daimler-Benz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daimler-motoren-gesellschaft.jpg" alt="Daimler-Motoren-Gesellschaft" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DMG-Werbung-1890.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
